.TH KERNEL_COMMAND_LINE 7 "March 2026" "Substrate" "Miscellaneous Information Manual"
.SH NAME
kernel_command_line \- Substrate kernel command-line parameters
.SH DESCRIPTION
Substrate accepts a whitespace-separated kernel command line from the bootloader.
Parameters are either boolean flags such as
.B serial_debug
or key/value pairs such as
.BR console=serial0 .
.PP
The
.B debug=
parameter enables named kernel debug channels without forcing every verbose
path on globally.
.SH SYNTAX
.BI debug= channel [ ,channel ... ]
.PP
Examples:
.IP \(bu 2
.B debug=syscall
.IP \(bu
.B debug=elf,perso:linux
.IP \(bu
.B debug=trap,perso:elks:aout
.IP \(bu
.B debug=storage:ide
.SH CHANNEL MATCHING
Channel names are colon-delimited.
An exact match enables that channel.
A parent channel enables all descendants.
.PP
Examples:
.IP \(bu 2
.B debug=perso:elks
matches
.B perso:elks
and
.B perso:elks:aout
.IP \(bu
.B debug=perso
matches any
.B perso:*
channel
.IP \(bu
.B debug=all
or
.B debug=*
enables every channel
.SH CURRENT CHANNELS
The current in-tree channels are:
.TP
.B syscall
Enable syscall entry/return tracing.
This is the structured replacement for the legacy
.B syscall_trace
and
.B syscall_log
boot flags.
.TP
.B elf
Enable verbose ELF loader and exec handoff tracing.
.TP
.B trap
Log user trap-to-signal translations before normal signal delivery.
.TP
.B proc
Log process-tree transitions and
.BR waitpid (2)
search decisions, including child-linking, exit, and reap flow.
.TP
.B storage:ide
Enable IDE transport diagnostics, including DMA setup and completion tracing.
.TP
.B vm:brk
Enable verbose
.BR brk (2)
/
.BR sbrk (2)
VM growth diagnostics.
.TP
.B perso:linux
Enable Linux-personality-specific loader diagnostics.
.TP
.B perso:elks
Enable ELKS personality diagnostics broadly.
This parent channel also enables more specific ELKS channels.
.TP
.B perso:elks:aout
Enable ELKS a.out loader tracing.
.TP
.B perso:elks:syscall
Enable ELKS unsupported-syscall diagnostics.
.TP
.B perso:elks:trap
Enable ELKS Minix trap diagnostics.
.TP
.B perso:elks:kmem
Enable ELKS synthetic
.B /dev/kmem
snapshot tracing, including exported task-slot order and kmem seek/read offsets.
.SH COMPATIBILITY
The following older boot flags remain supported:
.TP
.B syscall_trace
Equivalent to enabling the
.B syscall
channel.
.TP
.B syscall_log
Equivalent to enabling the
.B syscall
channel.
.PP
.B serial_debug
is separate from
.BR debug= .
It selects serial console mirroring; it does not by itself enable any debug
channel.
.SH RELATED PARAMETERS
.TP
.B console=console0
Use the default screen console.
.TP
.BI console=serial N
Route the console through COM\c
.IR N+1 .
.TP
.B video=text
Keep the system on the hardware text console and suppress framebuffer-console takeover.
.TP
.BI video=text: COLS x ROWS
Request a specific hardware text-console geometry.
This is equivalent to
.BR textmode= COLS x ROWS .
.TP
.BI textmode= COLS x ROWS
Select the hardware text-console geometry used by the kernel VT driver.
The bottom physical row is reserved for the kernel status line, so the visible tty geometry reported to userland is one row smaller than the selected physical mode.
On BIOS
.B zImage
and floppy boots, the setup stub applies supported text modes in real mode before entering the kernel proper.
.TP
.B vga=ask
On BIOS
.B zImage
and floppy boots, invoke the real-mode VGA text-mode selector before protected-mode handoff.
The current selector offers
.BR 80x25 ,
.BR 80x43 ,
and
.BR 80x50 .
When the BIOS advertises VBE text modes, the selector also adds any detected
.BR 132x25 ,
.BR 132x43 ,
.BR 132x50 ,
and
.BR 132x60
entries.
It then appends the matching
.B textmode=
token so the higher-half kernel uses the same geometry.
.PP
Currently supported kernel text-console geometries are:
.IP \(bu 2
.B 80x25
(visible tty area:
.BR 80x24 )
.IP \(bu
.B 80x43
(visible tty area:
.BR 80x42 )
.IP \(bu
.B 80x50
(visible tty area:
.BR 80x49 )
.PP
BIOS-selected text modes such as
.BR 80x43 ,
.BR 132x25 ,
.BR 132x43 ,
.BR 132x50 ,
and
.B 132x60
are honored after the real-mode setup path has programmed them.
The higher-half kernel does not fake those modes on its own; it only reprograms the stable built-in
.BR 80x25
and
.B 80x50
cases directly.
.TP
.BI root= device
Select the root block device.
.TP
.BI rootfstype= type [ ,type ... ]
Select one or more root filesystem probe targets.
.TP
.BI init= path
Select the initial userspace program.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR execve (2),
.BR signal (2),
.BR rootfs (7),
.BR personality_elks (7)
